Memory:</strong> 4 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Intel HD 3000 or better<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 1 GB available space</li></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system</li></ul>"},"platforms":{"linux":true,"mac":true,"windows":true},"price_overview":{"currency":"USD","discount_percent":0,"final":1999,"final_formatted":"$19.99 USD","initial":1999,"initial_formatted":""},"publishers":["All-Seeing Eye"],"ratings":{"dejus":{"banned":"0","descriptors":"Drogas l\u00edcitas\nLinguagem impr\u00f3pria\nAtos criminosos","rating":"12","rating_generated":"1","required_age":"12","use_age_gate":"0"},"steam_germany":{"banned":"0","descriptors":"Alkohol / Tabak\nSchimpfw\u00f6rte\nFantasy-Gewalt","rating":"12","rating_generated":"1","required_age":"12","use_age_gate":"0"}},"release_date":{"coming_soon":false,"date":"6 Oct, 2025"},"required_age":0,"reviews":"\u201cThe gameplay, visuals and humor feel very much like a love letter to Lucasarts classics. The UI is simple and easy to use (much like the Sam &amp; Max Max UI), the gag rate is high and there\u2019s lots of fun little surprises and easter eggs to discover. There are even some optional objectives to complete\u2026\u201d<br><strong>Alpha Beta Gamer</strong><br><br>\u201c...it\u2019s as if there was a get-together featuring the artists of LucasArts, 90s Nickelodeon cartoons, and Salvador Dali got together and did some acid. Presumably. The perspective in the game is unique and very reminiscent of 90s point and click adventures.\u201d<br><strong>Vulgar Knight</strong><br><br>\u201cI really enjoyed my time inside its world of spies, appreciating small nods to classic games and the inspirations drawn from them.\u201d<br><strong>A 90S KID</strong><br>","screenshots":[{"id":0,"path_full":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2117400/ss_c6cb5b2c